    "created_at": "2016-10-31T18:17:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-31T18:17:52Z",
    "body": "As far as I can tell the output didn't change in any bad ways. I think you could have leveraged link-defaults instead of sprinkling for=\"\" around but the source changes look good too. I guess these warnings really are a good thing, as it's good to be explicit about what e.g. `<a>index</a>` really is supposed to link to.\n",
