    "created_at": "2016-10-31T21:00:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-31T21:00:46Z",
    "body": "Yes, if you want future-proof turn on `Assume Explicit For` in your spec; then a missing `for` on an autolink is assumed to mean `for=/`, so you have to be explicit with every non-/ `for`.  You have to write more `for` values, but nothing can change under you.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
